\title "Chords panel mocks: the list, Insert, the editor"
\ts (4 4)
\chord ("G" 3 0 0 0 2 3)
\chord ("C" 0 1 0 2 3 x)
\chord ("D" 2 3 2 0 x x)
\chord ("Em" 0 0 0 2 2 0)
\chord ("Am" 0 1 2 2 0 x)
\chord ("Cadd9" 3 3 0 2 3 x)
\chord ("Dsus4" 3 3 2 0 x x)
\chord ("G/B" 3 0 0 0 2 x)
\chord ("F" 1 1 2 3 3 1)
\chord ("Bm" 2 3 4 4 2 x)
\section "1. The list"
(3.1 0.2 0.3 0.4 2.5 3.6).4{ch "G" txt "Tab view. Open the Chords panel (the last button in the rail on the left). Ten chords: the list scrolls (a), tiles (b) or one at a time (c). Switch with the Mock card, bottom right"}
  r.4 (0.1 1.2 0.3 2.4 3.5).4{ch "C"} r.4 |
\section "2. Fold"
(2.1 3.2 2.3 0.4).4{ch "D" txt "Double-click this D's diagram: its editor opens under the list. Press This track's chords: only the list folds, the editor stays. Press it again, then Cancel"}
  r.4 (0.1 0.2 0.3 2.4 2.5 0.6).4{ch "Em"} r.4 |
\section "3. Insert"
(0.1 1.2 2.3 2.4 0.5).4{ch "Am"} r.4{txt "Press this rest. In (a) press the arrow on Bm's row; in (b) and (c) pick Bm, then the Insert button (it names this place: bar 3, beat 2). Bm's notes and name land here"} (3.1 3.2 0.3 2.4 3.5).4{ch "Cadd9"} r.4 |
\section "4. Copy"
(3.1 3.2 2.3 0.4).4{ch "Dsus4" txt "Right-click C in the list (or the chord in (c)): Insert, Edit, Copy to new chord (Insert names the place when a column is picked). Press Copy to new chord: a New chord from C opens, named C 2, on C's shape. Pick another shape, press Add chord"}
  r.4 (3.1 0.2 0.3 0.4 2.5).4{ch "G/B"} r.4 |
\section "5. Editor"
r.1{txt "Add &chordeditor=shape to the link (or use the Mock card), then double-click G in the list: no Root or Type, only G's shapes and Change root and type. Press + : a new chord still shows Root and Type"} |
